{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/prometheus","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:08.024Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/azurelinux/base/prometheus/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/azurelinux/base/prometheus/about"},"readme":"## About\n\nThis repository contains the official Prometheus image for Azure Linux.\n\n### What is Azure Linux?\n\nAzure Linux is a Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. Azure Linux is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about Azure Linux, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is Prometheus?\n\nPrometheus is an application used for automated event monitoring and alerts, as well as collecting various time metrics. Prometheus is written in Go, but has libraries in many languages.\n\nSee: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prometheus_(software)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prometheus_(software)).\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `2`\n\nThe featured tags are multi-architecture tags (i.e., `x86-64` and `aarch64`) that refer to the latest version of the image. Additional tags that are specific to Prometheus version, Azure Linux build, or architecture can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Running a custom Prometheus server\n\n`1.` Run the Azure Linux Prometheus container image with custom config file mounted.\n\n    docker run -p <host port>:9090 \\\n               -v /<path to file>/prometheus.yml:/etc/prometheus \\\n               -it mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/prometheus:2\n    docker run -p <host port>:9090 \\\n               -v /<path to file>/prometheus.yml:/etc/prometheus \\\n               -it mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/distroless/prometheus:2\n\nThe default container startup command is `\"prometheus\", \"--config.file=/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml\"`. This launches prometheus with default settings.\n\n### Run a simple Prometheus server\n\nFor many simple Prometheus configs, you may find it inconvenient to write a complete prometheus.yml. In such cases, you can run the Azure Linux based Prometheus docker image directly:\n\n    docker run -p 9090:9090 -it mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/prometheus:2\n\n### Launch Azure Linux shell\n\nThe Prometheus image ships with a bash shell. The launch command can be provided to docker run command to Launch Azure Linux shell. The following command will launch the shell:\n\n    docker run -it --rm mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/prometheus:2 /bin/bash\n\n## Support\n\nAzure Linux container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe Azure Linux distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses included in the package sources available via srpm on [packages.microsoft.com](https://packages.microsoft.com/azurelinux/) or via our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-09-12T02:11:47.0590537+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"24K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"3.12","digest":"sha256:253ea74a5f7e9e1825df37b71d4ef26e355d08d43339d95c9de1962de2bb459e","pushed":"2026-09-12T01:19:48.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/v